  my_nite_rooteen: {
    "id": "my_nite_rooteen",
    "name": "My Nite Rooteen",
    "type": "data_log",
    "body": "MY NITE ROOTEEN\nby Amir (7 and a haf)\n\nMak sayd rite it down so I dont forget. So.\n\n1. Wash hands and face with the rain bukket. NOT drink it. Just face.\n\n2. Strech. Up to the sky and down to my toes. Mak says monsters cant catch a boy who is bendy.\n\n3. Look out the windo at the moon. Tonite it is very butiful and round like a roti canai nobody ate yet. If the moon is brite that is GOOD.\n\n4. PULL UP THE STAIRS. The ladder. All the way up. Before the jiant monsters come. Ah Moi next door forgot one time and now they dont live there anymore.\n\n5. Turn on the ISHTAR SHEILD. It is NEW!! Abah got it from the man with all the gold rings. It is a box with a green lite and it makes a noise but you cant hear the noise. Only the monsters can hear it and they HATE it. I put my ear on it and herd nothing. That means it is working Abah says.\n\n6. Abahs pistol is under the pillo but I am NOT ALOWED. But I know how. You pull safe tee. Then hold it with 2 hands. Then point at the monster not at Abah. Then pull the triger slow not fast. I think. I am not alowed.\n\n7. Say the prayer.\n\n8. Sleep.\n\nIf I do all of it and the moon is brite nothing will get me. Mak says. Mak is always rite except about sayur.\n\nThe End",
    "category_path": [
      "Found Texts",
      "Bandawang"
    ]
  },
  note_to_self_polish_the_axe: {
    "id": "note_to_self_polish_the_axe",
    "name": "Note to Self — Polish the Axe",
    "type": "data_log",
    "body": "NOTE TO SELF!!! (stick on mirror, NOT on fridge, Dol eats the notes on the fridge)\n\nPOLISH THE AXE BEFORE THE BATTLE OF THE BANDS. BEFORE. NOT AFTER. Last year you forgot and you went on looking like a busker at a pasar malam.\n\nHer name is Kak Ros. Pre-war electric, a Japanese copy of an American copy, cherry red where the red is left. Two strings out of six still working but who is counting. Neck glued back three times. Pickups dead since before my atuk. Frets filed down sharp like a parang all the way up to the twelfth — careful, member, CAREFUL when you do the solo.\n\nAnd the base. THE BASE. Three kilo of lead from the fishing weights at the Scrapyard, melted down in Dol's wok (sorry Dol), poured, cooled, and SOLDERED onto the butt of her body nice and slow, one bead at a time, smooth all round like the back of a spoon. Took me four nights. One swing and the other fella goes all jiwang. When I hit the high E she hums in my hands like she knows.\n\nBrasso: under the bed, left side.\nRag: NOT the rag with the engine oil. The other rag.\nAlso: new strap. Old strap is string.\n\nOur band kena lowest again this year so we are \"performing\" in the Battle. Manager says it's an honour. Manager is not performing.\n\nDoesn't matter. She will shine. Kak Ros always shines.\n\nROCK KAPAK SAMPAI MATI \\m/",
    "category_path": [
      "Found Texts",
      "Bandawang"
    ]
  },
