  selling_the_bar: {
    "id": "selling_the_bar",
    "name": "Selling the Bar",
    "type": "data_log",
    "body": "Thursday.\n\nHad a merchant in tonight, one of the long-haul men who runs Kulim to the Federation line and back. Northern accent, good boots. Paid in Protectorate dollars and tipped in them too, which nobody does, because nobody down here has change.\n\nHe got talking after the fourth glass. About Penang. The Fortress City. He's been inside, he says. Twice. As a vital merchant — which is a thing you can be, apparently, if you carry the right cargo and your papers have the right number on them.\n\nHot showers. That's what he started with. Not the walls, not the guns. Hot water out of a pipe, any hour, as long as you want. Rooms that stay cold inside when it's thirty-five degrees out. Lights that don't flicker when the man next door switches on his kettle. Streets swept by machines. Children in uniforms doing sums in classrooms with glass in the windows.\n\nAnd the wall. He drew it on the bar with his finger in the spilt beer. Warships, he said, old grey warships, stood up on their ends in the sea like somebody's giant had planted them, rusted together into one wall, with guns on top you can hear from Kedah when they practise.\n\nThen he stopped smiling. They're arrogant, he said. They look at you like a sum that won't come out. They let in the merchants they need and nobody else, and they don't pretend it's anything but that.\n\nI said I know the type. I serve them every week — the ones passing through, looking at my glasses like they're counting the germs.\n\nHe said: then you know. Don't go.\n\nFriday.\n\nPriced the bar. The stools, the fridge that works, the good glasses, the stock, the licence the Tans let me keep. Priced the room upstairs. Priced Ma's gold, which she said was for my wedding, which is not happening.\n\nIf I sell everything, I can buy a seat on a convoy North and still have enough left over to look like somebody's vital.\n\nHe said don't go.\n\nHe's been twice.",
    "category_path": [
      "Found Texts",
      "Bandawang"
    ]
  },
