  for_nora: {
    "id": "for_nora",
    "name": "For Nora",
    "type": "data_log",
    "body": "TELEKOM MALAYA — COUNTER VOICE MESSAGE — DELIVERY PENDING\nFrom: Hafiz (Butterworth depot, Penang yards)\nTo: Nora (Bandawang)\nLodged: 27 August 2077\n\n[recording]\n\nSayang. It's me. The line to the house is still down, so I'm leaving this at the telecom counter. They say it goes through when it goes through.\n\nI'm fine. Don't worry. Eat.\n\nOkay. I'll say it straight, because you'll hear it on the TV anyway — the TV in the canteen is on all day now.\n\nThe Americans in the yard have changed. Last month they were joking with us, buying us teh tarik, trying to say terima kasih. This week they don't talk to us. They took our passes for Dock 3. There are soldiers at the gates now, theirs, where our guards used to be. More ships come in every day and none of them need fixing.\n\nForeman says it's just security. Ah Leong says his cousin at the port heard that Washington thinks we're \"unreliable\". That we trade with the Chinese under the table. That there are \"elements\". And you know what they did to Canada. Everybody knows what they did to Canada.\n\nI'm scared, sayang. I'm scared they'll decide we are the same as China. That they'll look at our faces and see the enemy. That they'll stop asking to use our ports and just take them.\n\nMaybe it's nothing. Ah Leong also thinks the moon landing was fake, so.\n\nIf it's something — take Adik and go to your mother's. No. No, stay home. Stay home, fill the water tank, keep the radio on.\n\nI'll come home the minute they let us out. Tell Adik Abah is bringing back tambun biscuits from Penang. Tell him I didn't forget.\n\nI love you. They're saying time. I love you. Okay. I love —\n\n[recording ends]",
    "category_path": [
      "Found Texts",
      "Prewar Data Logs"
    ]
  },
  harapan_line_last_transmission: {
    "id": "harapan_line_last_transmission",
    "name": "Harapan Line — Last Transmission",
    "type": "data_log",
    "body": "[TRANSMISSION — HARAPAN LINE OPERATIONS CHANNEL — RECORDED OFF-AIR]\n\n[static]\n...Operations, Operations, this is Harapan Line, Train 9. Operations, do you read.\n\n[static]\n\nAnyone on this channel. Anyone. This is Rosli, Harapan Line driver. I am in the cab. The tunnel is down in front. It is down behind. Everything above us has come down. I can't move my legs, but I can talk. Radio is on the cab battery. Battery is good for some time.\n\nIf you can hear me, listen. Stay down. Don't go up to the surface. Whatever it is up there, don't go. Keep your water. Don't drink it fast. Look after each other.\n\n[pause]\n\nI don't think anyone is coming. It's all right. The cab is dry. I have half a packet of Marie biscuits.\n\nHasnah. Abang loves you. Aisyah, Imran, Daniel, Abah loves you very much. I'm sorry I'm late tonight. Hasnah, the motorbike is due for service. Don't let them overcharge. The school fees are in the biscuit tin on top of the fridge. The red tin, not the blue.\n\nI wanted to see Imran play on Sunday.\n\n[long pause]\n\nBattery light is orange now.\n\nAisyah, you always wanted me to bring you something from the big station. Next time.\n\n[pause]\n\nThis is Rosli, Harapan Line, Train 9, signing off.\n\n[recording ends]",
    "category_path": [
      "Found Texts",
      "Prewar Data Logs"
    ]
  },
  re_that_thing_you_asked_for: {
    "id": "re_that_thing_you_asked_for",
    "name": "Re: That Thing You Asked For",
    "type": "data_log",
    "body": "PROTIGA BERHAD — INTERNAL MAIL\nFROM: Rosnah Idris, Administrative Executive, Office of the Group Managing Director (Level 18)\nTO: [external address]\nDATE: 19 August 2077, 11:52 PM\nSUBJECT: Re: Re: Re: that thing you asked for\n\nSayang,\n\nFine. FINE. I've sent it. The spare for the B2 service door — the one from Datuk's drawer, not the Facilities one, because the Facilities ones are numbered and they count them every Friday. It's in a PosLaju envelope to the PO box you gave me. Please collect it before Monday. I have to put it back before audit and I cannot do this twice.\n\nI still don't understand why you can't just come up and I sign you in. You're the consultant! You have a lanyard! Why the PO box, why the envelope, why can't I just give it to you at lunch like a normal person?\n\nYou know what my week is like. Audit on Monday. Datuk shouting down the phone every hour — he thinks glass doors are soundproof. The east lift stuck between 11 and 12 with the tea lady in it. Aisyah from HR crying in the pantry, and when I asked what's wrong she said \"boy trouble\" and then she looked at me funny. Linda from Legal wearing perfume. LINDA. Everybody in this building is going mad.\n\nAnd my mother asking when you're coming to the house for dinner. I said you're busy. Are you busy? You're always busy.\n\nI'm not angry. I'm just tired. Tell me it's for what you said it's for. Tell me it's a surprise.\n\nDon't reply to this address. Reply to my personal.\n\nR.\n\n---- original message ----\nFROM: K.\nbabe its just so i can set up the surprise properly. u trust me right? pls. luv u <3",
    "category_path": [
      "Found Texts",
      "Prewar Data Logs"
    ]
  },
